2	Vocational Options After Class 10	After completing Class 10, students can move into a vocational higher secondary stream instead of the regular academic route. This option focuses more on hands-on skills, workshops and real workplace exposure, while still keeping the door open for further study later.	On this page you can explore different skill sectors, understand how admission works and discover important agencies and portals related to vocational education after Class 10.	[{"key":"Eligibility","value":"Passed Class 10"},{"key":"Duration","value":"Usually 2 years (equivalent to higher secondary in vocational stream)"},{"key":"Main Streams","value":"Business & Commerce, Engineering & Technology, Agriculture, Home Science"},{"key":"Typical Outcomes","value":"Early employability, eligibility for further vocational \\/ technical study, and a strong foundation for skill-based careers."}]	[{"code":"BC","title":"Business & Commerce","description":"Office, marketing and service roles for students who are comfortable with commerce, communication and people-facing work.","courses":["Marketing & salesmanship","Modern Office Practice","Library & Information Science","Travel & Tourism"]},{"code":"ET","title":"Engineering & Technology","description":"Job-oriented technical courses for those interested in machines, electronics, construction, IT and repair work.","courses":["Civil construction & Maintenance Technology","Automobile Mechanics","Air-Conditioner & Refrigerator mechanic","Computer Assembly & Maintenance","Pump Operator & Maintenance","IT Enabled Services","Maintenance & repair of Elec. Domestic Appliances","Consumer & Industrial Electronics Mechanics"]},{"code":"AG","title":"Agriculture","description":"Courses linked to farming, fisheries and plant-based livelihoods, suitable for rural students and those with land access.","courses":["Pisciculture","Dairy Farming","Preservation & Processing of Fruits & vegetables","Horticulture nursery management","Compost & vermicr