5	High-End Skill Training at MSME Tool Room, Kolkata	MSME Tool Room – Kolkata (Central Tool Room & Training Centre) is a Government of India society under the Ministry of MSME. It focuses on specialised training in tool & die making, CAD/CAM, automation, mechatronics, hardware and networking.	The programs below range from a 4-year diploma to focused certificate and advanced diploma courses of 2–6 months, meant for students after Class 10, ITI pass-outs, diploma holders and engineering graduates.	[{"key":"Institute","value":"MSME Tool Room \\u2013 Kolkata (Central Tool Room & Training Centre)"},{"key":"Authority","value":"Govt. of India Society, Ministry of MSME"},{"key":"Location","value":"Bon Hooghly Industrial Area, Kolkata \\u2013 700108"},{"key":"Website","value":"www.msmetoolroomkolkata.com"}]	[]	How to Choose the Right MSME Course	Next Steps	["If you have just passed Class 10 and want a full technical profession, consider the Diploma in Tool & Die Making.","If you are already in Diploma or B.Tech and want to specialise, look at CAD/CAM/CAE, Structural Design, VLSI & Embedded or Automation & Process Control.","If you enjoy machine shop and production work, consider CNC Machining and conventional machining programs.","If you are drawn towards computers, networks and servers, choose Hardware & Networking or CCNA-focused courses."]	["Match your interest with one of the groups above.","Check your eligibility (Class 10 / ITI / Diploma / Degree).","Note down duration, fee and start months.","Visit the official MSME Tool Room website to confirm the latest schedule and apply."]	[{"title":"MSME Tool Room – Kolkata (Central Tool Room & Training Centre)","subtitle":"Govt. of India Society, Ministry of MSME. Location: Bon Hooghly Industrial Area, Kolkata – 700108.","links":[{"label":"msmetoolroomkolkata.com","url":"http://www.msmetoolroomkolkata.com/"}]}]	4	t	2026-07-22 11:04:43	2026-07-25 04:04:15	30	31	32	36	courses/msme-tool-room-courses	[{"id": "diploma-tool-die", "fee": "₹36,000 per year", "name": "Diploma in Tool & Die Making (AICTE Approved)", "start": "August", "intake": "100", "summary": "Deep training in tool and die design, manufacturing processes and industrial practices through classroom and intensive workshop exposure.", "duration": "4 Years", "selection": "Test / Interview", "eligibility": "Class 10 pass (or equivalent) with Mathematics and Science, minimum 50% in aggregate (40% for SC/ST).", "contentsBrief": "Engineering Metrology, Workshop Technology, Engineering Drawing, Strength of Materials, Moulds, Press Tools, Jigs & Fixtures, manufacturing-related theory and practicals."}]	[{"id": "mcc-cadcam", "fee": "₹32,000", "name": "Master Certificate Course in CAD / CAM / CAE", "group": "Tool Design & CAD/CAM", "start": "February & August", "intake": "40", "contents": "Practice on AutoCAD, SolidWorks, Creo, CATIA, DELCAM, ANSYS and CNC programming using desktop simulators, CNC milling, CNC turning and WEDM.", "duration": "6 Months", "selection": "First Come – First Serve", "eligibility": "Degree in Engineering (Mechanical / Production / Manufacturing / Polymer or equivalent)."}, {"id": "mcc-structural", "fee": "₹25,000", "name": "Master Certificate Course in Structural Design and Analysis (MCSD-A)", "group": "Tool Design & CAD/CAM", "start": "February & August", "intake": "40", "contents": "AutoCAD, 3Ds Max, STAAD.Pro and Revit for structural modelling, visualisation and analysis.", "duration": "4 Months", "selection": "First Come – First Serve", "eligibility": "B.E. (Civil) or equivalent."}, {"id": "adv-tool-design-unknown-title", "fee": "Around ₹20,000 (see official notice for exact fee)", "name": "Advanced Tool Design Programme (course title partially unreadable in scan)", "note": "Exact course title and some details are not fully legible in the scan. Please cross-check with MSME Tool Room's latest prospectus.", "group": "Tool Design & CAD/CAM", "start": "February & August (as per scan)", "intake": "20–40 (as per batch size; check latest notice)", "contents": "Advanced work on moulds, press tools, jigs & fixtures and related manufacturing technology with AutoCAD, Delcam, Pro/E, SolidWorks and Creo.", "duration": "4 Months (as per scan)", "selection": "First Come – First Serve", "eligibility": "Diploma in Tool & Die Making / Mechanical Engineering or equivalent."}, {"id": "adv-cert-cnc", "fee": "₹32,000", "name": "Advance Certificate Course in CNC Machining", "group": "CNC & Conventional Machining", "start": "February, May, August & November", "intake": "40", "contents": "AutoCAD (2D), CNC part programming, Delcam (PowerMill), CNC turning, CNC milling and extensive shop-floor practice.", "duration": "6 Months", "selection": "First Come – First Serve", "eligibility": "Diploma (Mechanical) / ITI in Machinist, Tool & Die Maker, Grinder, Turner or equivalent."}, {"id": "conventional-machining-10th", "fee": "₹22,000", "name": "Conventional Lathe / Milling / Grinding Course (title not fully legible)", "note": "Course name line is partially corrupted in the scan; structure and contents are taken from the visible text.", "group": "CNC & Conventional Machining", "start": "January & July", "intake": "40", "contents": "Conventional lathe operations (threading, facing, drilling, reaming, taper turning, grooving, parting, boring, thread cutting), milling operations (plain, slab, face, angular, slot, gear and thread milling), grinding operations, bench work and drilling.", "duration": "6 Months", "selection": "First Come – First Serve", "eligibility": "10th Standard."}, {"id": "cert-mechatronics", "fee": "₹30,000", "name": "Certificate Course in Mechatronics", "group": "Automation, Mechatronics & Embedded", "start": "January & July", "intake": "40", "contents": "Basic electronics and applications, circuit design, basic electrical and industrial applications, electrical hardware control, industrial automation & PLC, interfacing with field devices, hydraulics & pneumatics, AutoCAD, digital electronics, VLSI & embedded concepts for office automation, CNC programming & practice, project work.", "duration": "6 Months", "selection": "First Come – First Serve", "eligibility": "ITI / Diploma in Electrical, Electronics, Mechanical, Instrument or equivalent."}, {"id": "cciam", "fee": "₹15,000", "name": "Certificate Course in Industrial Automation and Maintenance (CCIAM)", "group": "Automation, Mechatronics & Embedded", "start": "February & August", "intake": "40", "contents": "Electrical safety, basic electronics components and applications, electrical hardware control, industrial automation & PLC, interfacing with field devices, basics of hydraulics & pneumatics, industrial maintenance systems, computer fundamentals and CNC overview.", "duration": "3 Months", "selection": "First Come – First Serve", "eligibility": "ITI in Electrical / Electronics or equivalent."}, {"id": "mccapc", "fee": "₹22,000", "name": "Master Certificate Course in Automation & Process Control (MCCAPC)", "group": "Automation, Mechatronics & Embedded", "start": "February & August", "intake": "40", "contents": "Industrial automation with PLC, process control systems (including DCS and PID/PD/PI controllers), basic electronics and electricals, PLC programming and communication with field devices, project work.", "duration": "4 Months", "selection": "First Come – First Serve", "eligibility": "Diploma / Degree in Electrical, Electronics, Instrumentation, Mechanical or related fields (as per scan)."}, {"id": "admma", "fee": "₹20,000", "name": "Advance Diploma in Machine Maintenance & Automation (ADMMA)", "note": "Some lines on dates and detailed contents are not fully legible in the scan; confirm with current MSME Tool Room schedule.", "group": "Automation, Mechatronics & Embedded", "start": "Multiple batches in a year (as per notice)", "intake": "40", "contents": "Focus on maintenance of industrial machines, basics of automation and computer fundamentals with project work.", "duration": "4 Months", "selection": "First Come – First Serve", "eligibility": "Technical background (details partly unreadable; verify in prospectus)."}, {"id": "adves", "fee": "₹20,000", "name": "Advance Diploma in VLSI & Embedded System (ADVES)", "group": "Automation, Mechatronics & Embedded", "start": "February & August", "intake": "20", "contents": "Computer fundamentals, basic electronics & electricals, industrial automation & PLC, digital electronics, VLSI & embedded systems, microprocessor & microcontroller, basics of C language, VLSI circuit design with Microwind, Xilinx & Altera tools, ARM7, test equipment, basics of different types of robots, live practice and robotics project.", "duration": "4 Months", "selection": "First Come – First Serve", "eligibility": "Diploma / Degree in Electrical, Electronics, Mechanical, Instrument or equivalent."}, {"id": "cert-hardware-networking", "fee": "₹25,000", "name": "Certificate Course in Computer Hardware & Networking Management", "group": "Computer Hardware, Networking & CCNA", "start": "February & August", "intake": "40", "contents": "Computer fundamentals, basic electronics, SMPS and power supply, computer architecture, motherboard & add-on cards, microprocessor, storage devices, partitioning & OS loading, input devices, monitors, printers, system assembling, laptop overview; plus networking fundamentals, OSI model, protocols, topology, IP addressing, transmission media, cabling, peer-to-peer, client-server, DHCP, DNS, Linux networking and troubleshooting.", "duration": "6 Months", "selection": "First Come – First Serve", "eligibility": "Degree / Diploma (any discipline), any graduate, ITI, or 10+2."}, {"id": "adchnm-ccna", "fee": "As per latest fee schedule", "name": "Advance Diploma in Computer Hardware and Network Management with CCNA", "note": "Duration and some details are not fully readable; please confirm with MSME Tool Room Kolkata.", "group": "Computer Hardware, Networking & CCNA", "start": "February & August (as seen in scan)", "intake": "As per batch notification", "contents": "Extended training in computer hardware, network management and Cisco networking concepts, building on the certificate level course.", "duration": "Advanced long-term (duration not fully legible)", "selection": "First Come – First Serve", "eligibility": "Background in hardware / networking (exact line partly unreadable)."}, {"id": "ccna", "fee": "Fee varies by batch", "name": "Cisco Certified Network Associate (CCNA)", "note": "The scan shows overlapping CCNA blocks with slightly different values; follow the official MSME Tool Room notification for exact structure.", "group": "Computer Hardware, Networking & CCNA", "start": "Multiple batches (e.g., March, July, September, December).", "intake": "20", "contents": "Networking fundamentals, OSI model, IP addressing, VLSM, CIDR, routing & packet forwarding, router and switch configuration, static/dynamic routing (RIP, OSPF, EIGRP), switching technologies, VLAN and inter-VLAN routing, access lists and basic security, lab practice with Packet Tracer and Cisco devices.", "duration": "2–4 Months (varies by batch plan)", "selection": "First Come – First Serve", "eligibility": "Degree / Diploma (any discipline), BCA, MCA, 10+2 pass out."}]	{"url": "http://www.msmetoolroomkolkata.com/", "label": "Visit MSME Tool Room Website"}	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]
10	Diploma in Computer / IT	A Diploma in Computer / IT focuses on practical skills in computing, programming, networks, databases and office technology. It is designed to prepare students for entry-level roles in IT support, software development, office automation and related areas.	These diplomas are usually offered through polytechnics and technical institutes. They suit students who want a more hands-on, job-oriented route in technology, and can later connect to degree programmes such as B.Tech, BCA or B.Sc in Computer Science / IT.	[{"key":"Eligibility","value":"Commonly after Class 10 or Class 12, depending on the diploma and institute. Mathematics is often required or strongly recommended."},{"key":"Duration","value":"Around 3 years for core diplomas; shorter durations for some application \\/ software courses."},{"key":"Course Types","value":"Core computer engineering, software development, office applications, graphics and multimedia."},{"key":"Work Area","value":"IT support, junior developer roles, data entry & MIS, lab\\/office IT maintenance, design & multimedia teams."},{"key":"Progression","value":"Lateral or regular entry into B.Tech \\/ BE (CSE \\/ IT), BCA, B.Sc (CS \\/ IT), followed by MCA or M.Tech."}]	[]	Admission & Where to Study	\N	[\n        "Many 3-year Computer / IT diplomas are available after Class 10 through polytechnic / technical entrance exams.",\n        "For some programmes (especially more advanced or software-focused diplomas), Class 12 with Mathematics or a Science stream background is preferred.",\n        "In many states, there are also lateral-entry options into second year diploma for ITI / vocational students, depending on current rules.",\n        "Exact eligibility (subjects, marks, age) and admission mode (entrance test vs. direct admission) are decided by each board / institution, so students must always check the latest notifications."\n    ]	[]	[]	10	t	2026-07-22 15:31:25	2026-07-25 04:09:36	30	37	38	42	courses/diploma-i