11	About Arts Graduation Courses	Arts graduation is one of the most flexible degree routes after Class 12. It can be built around a major subject (Honours) or a broader combination (General), and it works well for higher studies, competitive exams, teaching pathways, and diverse entry-level careers.	In streamlined Arts-aligned choices, you'll commonly see B.A, B.A Public Administration, Integrated B.A LL.B (Law), and BSW (Social Work). The right choice depends on your long-term goal—so decide early and build skills + experience alongside your degree.	[{"key":"Options covered","value":"BA \\u2022 Public Admin \\u2022 BA LL.B \\u2022 BSW"},{"key":"Typical duration","value":"3 years (most UG) \\u2022 5 years (Integrated Law)"},{"key":"Entry","value":"After Class 12"},{"key":"Admission","value":"Merit \\/ Entrance (varies by institute)"},{"key":"Good for","value":"PG \\u2022 Exams \\u2022 Teaching track \\u2022 Careers"}]	[]	\N	\N	[]	[]	[]	11	t	2026-07-22 15:51:03	2026-07-25 04:11:15	30	43	44	45	courses/arts-graduation-courses-ba-allied	[]	[]	{}	[]	[]	[]	[{"items": ["Bengali", "English", "Hindi", "Urdu", "Sanskrit", "Other languages"], "title": "Languages & Literature"}, {"items": ["History", "Philosophy", "Geography"], "title": "Humanities"}, {"items": ["Political Science", "Sociology", "Psychology", "Public Administration"], "title": "Social Sciences"}, {"items": ["Economics (General/Honours depending on institute)"], "title": "Economics"}]	[{"id": "ba-general", "tag": "BA", "level": "UG", "title": "B.A (General)", "description": "Broad combinations. Good if you want flexibility and multiple direction options."}, {"id": "ba-honours", "tag": "BA", "level": "UG", "title": "B.A (Honours)", "description": "One major subject. Better if you plan PG/teaching/research in the same domain."}, {"id": "ba-addons", "tag": "Add-ons", "level": "Must", "title": "Skills & Experience", "description": "Communication + basic digital skills + internship/volunteering improve outcomes sharply."}]	[]	[{"desc": "MA / MSW / other PG → specialization and better opportunities.", "title": "Higher Studies", "points": ["Pick a subject you can continue long-term (MA/research).", "Improve writing, reading depth and basic research skills.", "Build a clean academic profile (attendance + grades)."]}, {"desc": "Plan UG + required teaching qualification for school/education roles.", "title": "Teaching Track", "points": ["Choose a strong Honours subject for your teaching domain.", "Work on communication and classroom confidence early.", "Check eligibility rules for teaching roles before deciding."]}, {"desc": "WBCS/UPSC/SSC/Banking/Railways — choose based on interest & eligibility.", "title": "Competitive Exams", "points": ["Build GK + current affairs habit (daily, not last-minute).", "Choose one exam track and stick to it for 6–12 months.", "Practice answer writing / mocks consistently."]}, {"desc": "Communication, digital skills, internships → faster employability.", "title": "Skill + Job Route", "points": ["MS Office / Docs + presentations (must-have for most jobs).", "English + interview practice + resume basics.", "Internship/volunteering for real experience and confidence."]}]	["Many UG admissions are based on Class 12 marks (merit list).", "Some colleges may have subject cut-offs or entrance routes for selected courses.", "Always verify from official institute/university notices before applying."]	["Class 10 & 12 marksheets", "ID proof (Aadhaar etc.)", "Photo + signature", "Category/EWS/Income certificate (if applicable)", "Domicile (if required)"]	[{"title": "Govt Exams Track", "description": "WBCS/UPSC/SSC etc. (based on your goal)"}, {"title": "Teaching/Education", "description": "BA + required teaching qualification path"}, {"title": "Administration", "description": "Office/admin/coordinator roles with skills"}, {"title": "Media/Content", "description": "Content, communication, social media (with add-ons)"}, {"title": "Social Sector/NGO", "description": "Community programs, CSR, field/project work"}, {"title": "Higher Studies", "description": "MA/MSW → research/academics specialization"}]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]
12	About Commerce Graduation Courses	Commerce graduation is the most direct route into accounting, finance, banking and business operations. Students typically choose B.Com (General/Honours) as the core degree and then strengthen outcomes with professional courses, skill training, internships and a clear career goal.	In streamlined Commerce choices, the main UG route is B.Com (General/Honours), supported by allied options like BBA (management-focused) and finance/accounting specialisation degrees offered by some institutes. Your final outcome depends heavily on skills (Excel/communication) and practical exposure.	[{"key":"Main course","value":"B.Com (General \\/ Honours)"},{"key":"Allied options","value":"BBA \\u2022 Finance\\/Accounting specialisations \\u2022 Economics (where available)"},{"key":"Typical duration","value":"3 years"},{"key":"Entry","value":"After Class 12"},{"key":"Good for","value":"Accounts \\u2022 Finance \\u2022 Banking \\u2022 Business \\u2022 Exams"}]	[]	\N	\N	[]	[]	[]	0	t	2026-07-22 16:03:43	2026-07-25 04:12:29	30	43	44	46	courses/commerce-graduation-courses-bcom-allied	[]	[]	{}	[]	[]	[]	[{"items": ["Financial Accounting", "Business Studies", "Commerce Basics"], "title": "Core Commerce"}, {"items": ["Corporate Finance", "Taxation basics", "Costing basics"], "title": "Finance & Tax"}, {"items": ["Marketing basics", "HR fundamentals", "Operations overview"], "title": "Management"}, {"items": ["Excel", "Communication", "Presentation", "Internship exposure"], "title": "Skills (must add)"}]	[{"id": "bcom-general-honours", "tag": "B.Com", "icon": "Calculator", "level": "UG", "title": "B.Com (General / Honours)", "description": "The most common Commerce degree. Honours gives depth (Accounting/Finance), while General keeps options wide. Best for accounting, finance, banking support roles and business foundation; a strong base for CA/CS/CMA and MBA preparation, with good progression to M.Com, MBA/PGDM and professional certifications. Duration: 3 years; Eligibility: Class 12 pass (Commerce preferred)."}, {"id": "bba-ug-management", "tag": "BBA", "icon": "Briefcase", "level": "UG", "title": "BBA (UG Management)", "description": "A management-focused UG route for business operations, marketing, HR and entrepreneurship basics. Best for an early management track (marketing/HR/operations) and works well before MBA/PGDM — internships and communication skills matter a lot. Duration: 3 years; Eligibility: Class 12 pass."}, {"id": "bcom-specialisations", "tag": "B.Com", "icon": "PieChart", "level": "UG", "title": "B.Com (Accounting & Finance / similar specialisations)", "description": "Commerce specialisations offered by some institutes. Names differ, but focus stays around finance, accounting and taxation basics — more focused than B.Com General, good for finance roles and professional course support. Check curriculum and placement exposure of the institute. Duration: 3 years; Eligibility: Class 12 pass."}, {"id": "ba-bsc-economics", "tag": "Economics", "icon": "Landmark", "level": "UG", "title": "B.A / B.Sc Economics (where available)", "description": "Economics is a strong allied route for commerce-minded students, supporting banking, analytics, policy and higher studies. Strong base for banking/finance and an analytics mindset, good for competitive exams and higher studies; skill add-ons (Excel/data) boost outcomes. Duration: 3 years; Eligibility: Class 12 pass."}]	[]	[{"desc": "CA / CS / CMA and other certifications build strong career advantage.", "title": "Professional Courses", "points": ["Choose one professional track early and stay consistent", "Build accounting + law basics gradually (don't rush)", "Practice mock tests and problem solving regularly"]}, {"desc": "M.Com / MBA / specialised PG routes for better roles and growth.", "title": "Higher Studies", "points": ["M.Com for deeper commerce + academic path", "MBA for management roles and leadership track", "Short courses (Excel, Tally, analytics) help alongside"]}, {"desc": "Banking/SSC/Railways/state exams — commerce gives good base for aptitude & GK.", "title": "Competitive Exams", "points": ["Strengthen aptitude (math/reasoning) + English", "Follow current affairs daily", "Practice mocks and previous year papers"]}, {"desc": "Accounts assistant, billing, operations, sales support roles grow fast with skills.", "title": "Skill + Job Route", "points": ["Excel + basic accounting tools", "Resume + interview practice", "Internships / part-time experience helps a lot"]}]	["Many UG admissions are based on Class 12 marks (merit list).", "Some colleges may have subject cut-offs or entrance routes for selected programmes.", "Always verify from official institute/university notices before applying."]	["Class 10 & 12 marksheets", "ID proof (Aadhaar etc.)", "Photo + signature", "Category/EWS/Income certificate (if applicable)", "Domicile (if required)"]	[{"title": "Accounts & Finance", "description": "Accounting, billing, finance support, junior analyst roles"}, {"title": "Banking & Exams", "description": "Bank PO/Clerk, insurance, SSC, state-level exams"}, {"title": "Business Operations", "description": "Operations/admin/coordinator roles with Excel + communication"}, {"title": "Sales & Marketing", "description": "Sales support, marketing operations, business development entry roles"}, {"title": "Professional Practice", "description": "CA/CS/CMA track → audit, taxation, compliance"}, {"title": "Management Track", "description": "BBA/MBA path → HR, marketing, operations leadership"}]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]
16	About Arts Post Graduation	Arts postgraduate study helps you go deeper into a subject and improve long-term career outcomes. It is most useful when you have a clear goal—teaching, research, social sector careers, policy/administration, or competitive exam preparation.	In streamlined Arts PG routes, the most common options are M.A (subject masters), M.S.W (professional social work), and other allied PG programmes in humanities and social sciences depending on the university.	[{"key":"Main PG routes","value":"MA \\u2022 MSW \\u2022 Allied Arts PG"},{"key":"Typical duration","value":"2 years"},{"key":"Entry","value":"After graduation"},{"key":"Best for","value":"Teaching \\u2022 Research \\u2022 NGO\\/CSR \\u2022 Exams"},{"key":"Key success factor","value":"Projects\\/fieldwork + writing + clarity"}]	[]	\N	\N	[]	[]	[]	0	t	2026-07-23 07:28:14	2026-07-25 04:16:42	30	43	48	49	courses/arts-pg-courses-ma-msw-allied	[]	[]	{}	[]	[]	[]	[{"items": ["Bengali", "English", "Hindi", "Urdu", "Sanskrit", "Other languages"], "title": "Languages & Literature"}, {"items": ["History", "Philosophy", "Geography"], "title": "Humanities"}, {"items": ["Political Science", "Sociology", "Psychology", "Public Administration"], "title": "Social Sciences"}, {"items": ["Economics", "Development studies (where available)"], "title": "Economics & Interdisciplinary"}]	[{"id": "ma-masters", "tag": "MA", "icon": "GraduationCap", "level": "PG", "title": "M.A (Master of Arts)", "description": "The most common Arts postgraduate degree. It deepens your subject knowledge and supports teaching, research and competitive exam preparation. Best for subject depth, academics and long-term specialization; useful for the teaching track and higher studies (PhD/research), and also supports competitive exams and policy/administration roles depending on subject. Duration: 2 years (typical); Eligibility: Graduation (subject rules vary)."}, {"id": "msw-social-work", "tag": "MSW", "icon": "Users", "level": "PG", "title": "M.S.W (Master of Social Work)", "description": "A professional PG route for social sector careers. Strong for NGO leadership, development projects, counselling support and CSR roles. Best progression after BSW, but open to other graduates too (as per rules); fieldwork/internships are central to MSW outcomes and lead to program management, CSR, community development roles. Duration: 2 years (typical); Eligibility: Graduation (rules vary)."}, {"id": "allied-arts-pg", "tag": "Allied", "icon": "ScrollText", "level": "PG", "title": "Allied Arts PG (subject-wise masters)", "description": "Many universities offer PG programmes aligned to Arts & social sciences—examples include Public Administration, Sociology, Political Science, Psychology and more. Choose based on long-term career goal (teaching/research/governance/social sector); subject choice matters more than degree name alone, so build projects, writing and field exposure during PG. Duration: 2 years (typical); Eligibility: Graduation (subject mapping varies)."}]	[]	[{"desc": "PG builds subject depth and improves eligibility for academic roles (as per norms).", "title": "Teaching & Academics", "points": ["Strong writing + conceptual clarity matters most", "Choose dissertation/project topics carefully", "Follow eligibility rules for teaching recruitment"]}, {"desc": "For students who enjoy deep study and research work in a subject domain.", "title": "Research Path (PhD / Fellowships)", "points": ["Develop research writing + methodology basics", "Build a clean academic profile + references", "Track fellowships and university research admissions"]}, {"desc": "Field-based careers in NGOs, CSR foundations, development and community programs.", "title": "Social Sector / CSR (MSW focus)", "points": ["Internships/fieldwork is the real differentiator", "Build program documentation + reporting skills", "Leadership grows with experience + networks"]}, {"desc": "PG strengthens your subject base for exams and policy/governance work.", "title": "Competitive Exams & Policy Roles", "points": ["Answer writing and reading depth improves results", "Select optional subject wisely (if applicable)", "Stay consistent with current affairs + core concepts"]}]	["PG admissions can be merit-based or entrance-based depending on the university.", "Some subjects require graduation in the same/related discipline; rules vary by institute.", "Check reservation/category rules and domicile requirements where applicable."]	["Graduation marksheets / final result", "Class 10 & 12 marksheets", "ID proof (Aadhaar etc.)", "Photo + signature", "Category/EWS/Income certificate (if applicable)", "Migration/TC (if asked by institute)"]	[{"title": "Teaching Track", "description": "Lecturer/teaching pathway (as per eligibility) + coaching/academic roles"}, {"title": "Research & PhD", "description": "PhD, research assistant/project roles, fellowships"}, {"title": "NGO / CSR", "description": "Program officer, project coordinator, CSR roles (MSW strong)"}, {"title": "Policy & Governance", "description": "Policy support, administration roles, think tanks (subject dependent)"}, {"title": "Content / Communication", "description": "Writing, communication, media + social sector comms"}, {"title": "Competitive Exams", "description": "State/national exams supported by deep subject base"}]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]
14	About Commerce Post Graduation	Commerce postgraduate study builds advanced knowledge in accounting, finance, taxation and business systems. It is best suited for students targeting teaching, finance roles, professional courses or research in commerce-related areas.	In streamlined Commerce PG routes, M.Com is the primary option, supported by specialised and allied PG programmes depending on university offerings. Outcomes improve significantly with practical tools, internships and a clear career goal.	[{"key":"Main PG route","value":"M.Com (General \\/ Specialised)"},{"key":"Typical duration","value":"2 years"},{"key":"Entry","value":"After graduation (Commerce-related)"},{"key":"Best for","value":"Teaching \\u2022 Finance \\u2022 Research \\u2022 Exams"},{"key":"Key success factor","value":"Tools + internships + clarity"}]	[]	\N	\N	[]	[]	[]	0	t	2026-07-23 07:15:01	2026-07-25 04:13:50	30	43	48	50	courses/commerce-pg-courses-mcom-allied	[]	[]	{}	[]	[]	[]	[{"items": ["Advanced Accounting", "Corporate Finance", "Financial Management"], "title": "Accounting & Finance"}, {"items": ["Direct & Indirect Taxes", "Business Law", "Corporate Compliance"], "title": "Taxation & Law"}, {"items": ["Business Economics", "Statistics", "Research Methods"], "title": "Economics & Analytics"}, {"items": ["Advanced Excel", "Accounting software", "Presentation & reporting"], "title": "Skills (must add)"}]	[{"id": "mcom-general", "tag": "M.Com", "icon": "Calculator", "level": "PG", "title": "M.Com (General / Accounting / Finance)", "description": "Postgraduate commerce degree focused on accounting, finance, taxation and advanced commerce concepts. Best for accounting, finance, teaching and academic tracks; a strong base for CA/CS/CMA support, finance roles and PhD/research in commerce-related subjects. Duration: 2 years (typical); Eligibility: B.Com / related graduation."}, {"id": "mcom-specialised", "tag": "M.Com", "icon": "PieChart", "level": "PG", "title": "M.Com (Specialised streams)", "description": "Some universities offer specialisations like Accounting & Finance, Taxation, Banking, or Management, with a more focused curriculum than M.Com General — good for niche finance, taxation and compliance roles. Check syllabus and faculty strength before choosing. Duration: 2 years (typical); Eligibility: Commerce-related graduation."}, {"id": "allied-commerce-pg", "tag": "Allied", "icon": "Briefcase", "level": "PG", "title": "Allied Commerce PG", "description": "Allied PG programmes related to commerce such as Business Economics, Banking & Insurance, or Management-focused masters. Choose based on career goal (industry/academics/exams); skill-oriented PGs work best with internships and practical exposure. Duration: 2 years (typical); Eligibility: Graduation (rules vary)."}]	[]	[{"desc": "M.Com strengthens eligibility and subject depth for academic roles (as per norms).", "title": "Teaching & Academics", "points": ["Build strong conceptual clarity and academic writing", "Choose dissertation topic aligned with long-term plan", "Track teaching eligibility and recruitment rules"]}, {"desc": "M.Com complements CA/CS/CMA preparation and finance certifications.", "title": "Professional Courses Support", "points": ["Align PG subjects with professional syllabus", "Practice problem-solving consistently", "Balance PG + professional prep carefully"]}, {"desc": "Finance, accounts, compliance, operations and analyst roles.", "title": "Industry & Corporate Roles", "points": ["Internships and practical tools matter", "Advanced Excel + accounting software helps", "Documentation and communication improve growth"]}, {"desc": "Commerce PG supports exams in banking, finance and administration.", "title": "Competitive Exams", "points": ["Focus on aptitude + finance basics", "Stay consistent with current affairs", "Practice mocks and previous papers"]}]	["M.Com admissions may be merit-based or entrance-based depending on university.", "Some specialisations require specific UG background; mapping varies.", "Check institute accreditation, faculty and dissertation structure."]	["Graduation marksheets / final result", "Class 10 & 12 marksheets", "ID proof (Aadhaar etc.)", "Photo + signature", "Category/EWS/Income certificate (if applicable)", "Migration/TC (if required)"]	[{"title": "Teaching Track", "description": "Commerce teaching and academic roles (as per eligibility)"}, {"title": "Finance & Accounts", "description": "Accounting, finance, audit and compliance roles"}, {"title": "Professional Practice", "description": "CA/CS/CMA aligned roles and support"}, {"title": "Corporate & Operations", "description": "Business operations, reporting and analyst roles"}, {"title": "Research & PhD", "description": "PhD, research assistant and academic research paths"}, {"title": "Competitive Exams", "description": "Banking, finance and administrative exams"}]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]
17	About Science Post Graduation	Science postgraduate study is about specialization and depth. It works best for students who want research, teaching, technical roles, or a strong subject foundation for higher studies and competitive technical exams.	In streamlined science PG routes, the main option is M.Sc (subject masters), with allied pathways like Mathematics/Statistics, Computer Science/IT (where offered), and other applied science programmes. Outcomes improve sharply when you build projects, lab skills and practical tool exposure.	[{"key":"Main PG route","value":"M.Sc (subject masters)"},{"key":"Allied options","value":"Maths\\/Stats \\u2022 CS\\/IT \\u2022 Applied sciences"},{"key":"Typical duration","value":"2 years"},{"key":"Entry","value":"After graduation (B.Sc\\/related)"},{"key":"Best for","value":"Research \\u2022 Teaching \\u2022 Technical roles"}]	[]	\N	\N	[]	[]	[]	0	t	2026-07-23 07:29:48	2026-07-25 04:18:34	30	43	48	51	courses/science-pg-courses-msc-allied	[]	[]	{}	[]	[]	[]	[{"items": ["Physics", "Chemistry", "Electronics", "Environmental Science"], "title": "Physical Sciences"}, {"items": ["Botany", "Zoology", "Microbiology", "Biotechnology"], "title": "Life Sciences"}, {"items": ["Mathematics", "Statistics"], "title": "Mathematical Sciences"}, {"items": ["Computer Science", "IT", "Data-focused masters (where offered)"], "title": "Computing"}]	[{"id": "msc-core-sciences", "tag": "M.Sc", "icon": "FlaskConical", "level": "PG", "title": "M.Sc (Core Sciences)", "description": "Postgraduate specialization in a science subject. Ideal for deeper subject mastery, research readiness and technical roles. Best for strong specialization and lab/research exposure, a good base for PhD/research projects (subject dependent), and also supports the teaching track and scientific roles. Duration: 2 years (typical); Eligibility: B.Sc / related graduation (rules vary)."}, {"id": "msc-maths-statistics", "tag": "M.Sc", "icon": "Calculator", "level": "PG", "title": "M.Sc Mathematics / Statistics", "description": "Advanced quantitative PG route for research, analytics, teaching and data-heavy careers. Strong base for a data/analytics mindset and quantitative roles, good for higher studies and research in mathematical sciences; requires consistent practice and conceptual depth. Duration: 2 years (typical); Eligibility: B.Sc with Maths/Stats (rules vary)."}, {"id": "msc-computer-science-it", "tag": "M.Sc", "icon": "Monitor", "level": "PG", "title": "M.Sc Computer Science / IT (where offered)", "description": "PG computing route for software/data careers and advanced computing roles. Outcomes depend heavily on projects and skills — good for software/data paths with strong projects; internship and portfolio matter as much as the degree, so choose institutes with labs, faculty support and exposure. Duration: 2 years (typical); Eligibility: B.Sc/BCA/related (rules vary)."}, {"id": "allied-science-pg", "tag": "Allied", "icon": "Microscope", "level": "PG", "title": "Allied Science PG (subject-wise masters)", "description": "Universities also offer allied science PG programmes such as Biotechnology, Microbiology, Environmental Science, Electronics and more. Choose based on career goal (industry/research/teaching), check lab facilities and practical exposure of the institute; projects and internships improve outcomes sharply. Duration: 2 years (typical); Eligibility: Related graduation (mapping varies)."}]	[]	[{"desc": "Best for students who enjoy deep study and research work. MSc is a strong bridge to PhD.", "title": "Research Path (PhD / Projects / Fellowships)", "points": ["Develop research writing + methodology basics", "Build 1–2 serious projects/dissertation work", "Track fellowships and university PhD notifications"]}, {"desc": "MSc improves subject depth and supports teaching readiness (as per eligibility norms).", "title": "Teaching & Academics", "points": ["Conceptual clarity + problem solving matters", "Build lab and demonstration co