19	MBBS & Core Medical Degrees	MBBS is the primary medical degree required to become a doctor in India. It focuses on diagnosis, treatment, patient care and clinical decision-making across all major medical disciplines.	It is a long and demanding journey, where real career growth comes after postgraduate specialisation and sustained clinical experience.	[{"key":"Degree type","value":"Core Medical (Doctor) Degree"},{"key":"Duration","value":"4.5 Years + 1 Year Internship"},{"key":"Entrance exam","value":"NEET (UG)"},{"key":"Next levels","value":"MD \\/ MS \\u2192 DM \\/ MCh"},{"key":"Reality check","value":"PG specialisation decides growth"}]	[{"code":null,"title":null,"description":null,"courses":[null]}]	\N	\N	[null]	[null]	[{"title":null,"subtitle":null,"links":[{"label":null,"url":null}]}]	19	t	2026-07-23 11:22:37	2026-07-25 04:21:52	30	52	53	55	courses/medical/mbbs	[]	[]	{}	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[{"title": "Government Hospitals", "description": "Medical Officer, Resident Doctor, Specialist roles through state/central services."}, {"title": "Private Hospitals", "description": "Clinical practice, emergency care, ICU, speciality departments."}, {"title": "Medical Colleges", "description": "Teaching, training, academic medicine (after PG)."}, {"title": "Public Health & Administration", "description": "Health services, programmes, policy and administration (with experience)."}]	[]	[]	["Strong academic foundation + disciplined study routine", "Serious clinical exposure during postings & internship", "Communication skills and ethical patient handling", "Stress management and long-hour work readiness", "Early clarity on PG specialisation goals"]	[{"focus": "Foundation of medical sciences, clinical diagnosis, patient care and hospital-based training.", "title": "MBBS (Bachelor of Medicine & Bachelor of Surgery)", "duration": "4.5 Years"}, {"focus": "Hands-on rotational training across Medicine, Surgery, OBG, Paediatrics, Emergency and allied departments.", 