ing)"]}, {"key": "radiology", "badge": "Imaging & Patient Safety", "title": "Radiology & Imaging (Diploma / B.Sc / M.Sc)", "bestFor": "Students who like medical technology, imaging systems workflow and structured clinical department routines.", "whatYouDo": "Support imaging services like X-ray and advanced imaging workflow (as per training and centre policy).", "commonRoutes": ["Diploma (entry)", "B.Sc Imaging / Radiology (UG)", "M.Sc Imaging (PG)"], "whereYouWork": ["Hospitals", "Imaging centres", "Diagnostic chains", "Speciality clinics"]}, {"key": "ot", "badge": "OT Systems & Sterility", "title": "Operation Theatre & Anaesthesia Technology (Diploma / B.Sc / M.Sc)", "bestFor": "Students who can handle pressure, protocols and sterile discipline, and like structured OT environments.", "whatYouDo": "Assist OT workflows: sterilisation protocols, instruments handling, OT preparation and anaesthesia support systems (as per scope).", "commonRoutes": ["Diploma (entry)", "B.Sc OT & Anaesthesia (UG)", "M.Sc OT/AT (PG)"], "whereYouWork": ["Hospitals (OT)", "Surgical centres", "Emergency & trauma units"]}]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]
28	About B.Tech / B.E	B.Tech (Bachelor of Technology) and B.E (Bachelor of Engineering) are undergraduate professional degrees focused on applying science, mathematics and technology to solve real-world problems. These programs combine classroom learning, laboratory work, projects and internships, preparing students for engineering roles across IT, core industries, infrastructure and emerging technologies.	These programs combine classroom learning, laboratory work, projects and internships, preparing students for engineering roles across IT, core industries, infrastructure and emerging technologies.	[\n        {"key":"Degree type","value":"Professional Engineering Degree"},\n        {"key":"Duration","value":"4 Years"},\n        {"key":"Eligibility","value":"Class 12 (PCM)"},\n        {"key":"Entry exams","value":"JEE / State-level / Institute exams"},\n        {"key":"Career scope","value":"Industry • PSU • Higher studies • Startups"}\n    ]	[]	\N	\N	[]	[]	[]	28	t	2026-07-23 18:44:16	2026-07-23 18:46:19	30	66	67	68	courses/btech-be-programs	[]	[]	{}	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[{"icon": "Cpu", "title": "IT & Software Industry", "description": "Software development, data roles, system engineering, tech services."}, {"icon": "Factory", "title": "Core Engineering Industries", "description": "Manufacturing, power, electronics, telecom, automotive, infrastructure."}, {"icon": "Wrench", "title": "Construction & Infrastructure", "description": "Civil projects, design, execution, quality, planning roles."}, {"icon": "Briefcase", "title": "Corporate / Consulting / Startups", "description": "Product companies, startups, analytics, operations, tech consulting."}]	["Choose colleges with strong labs, faculty and placement records.", "Branch matters, but skills and projects matter more in the long run.", "Internships during 2nd–4th year significantly improve outcomes."]	["Class 10 & 12 marksheets", "Entrance exam admit card & rank card", "ID proof (Aadhaar etc.)", "Photo + signature", "Category/EWS/Income certificate (if applicable)", "Domicile certificate (if required)"]	["Strong fundamentals in maths, logic and core subjects", "Hands-on projects beyond syllabus", "Internships (industry or research based)", "Programming + problem-solving skills (for most branches)", "Communication skills and teamwork mindset"]	[]	["Class 12 passed with Physics, Chemistry and Mathematics (PCM).", "Admission generally through entrance exams (JEE, state-level exams or institute exams).", "Eligibility criteria, age limits and counselling rules vary by exam and institute.", "Medical fitness and document verification apply as per admission rules."]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[{"focus": "Core engineering foundation with theory, labs, projects and industrial exposure.", "title": "B.Tech / B.E (Undergraduate Engineering)", "duration": "4 Years"}, {"focus": "Software, core engineering, manufacturing, infrastructure, PSU/private sector roles.", "title": "Industry / Job / Startup", "duration": "Immediate after UG"}, {"focus": "Advanced specialisation, research orientation, higher technical roles.", "title": "M.Tech / M.E (Postgraduate)", "duration": "2 Years"}, {"focus": "Senior engineering roles, R&D, teaching, technical leadership, entrepreneurship.", "title": "Research / Leadership Growth", "duration": "Continuous"}]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	["Computer Science & Engineering (CSE)", "Information Technology (IT)", "Electronics & Communication Engineering (ECE)", "Electrical Engineering (EE)", "Mechanical Engineering (ME)", "Civil Engineering (CE)", "Artificial Intelligence / Data Science (emerging branches)", "Chemical / Instrumentation / Production (as offered)"]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]
26	AYUSH (Ayurveda, Homoeopathy, Unani, Siddha)	AYUSH represents India's recognized traditional and alternative medical systems — Ayurveda, Homoeopathy, Unani and Siddha. These are doctor-level clinical pathways within their own systems, with UG degrees and internships followed by PG specialisation options.	Success in AYUSH depends on clinical discipline, ethics, patient communication and consistent practice building — similar to other medical careers, but within the philosophy and methods of the chosen system.	[{"key":"Systems covered","value":"Ayurveda \\u2022 Homoeopathy \\u2022 Unani \\u2022 Siddha"},{"key":"Main UG degrees","value":"BAMS \\u2022 BHMS \\u2022 BUMS \\u2022 BSMS"},{"key":"Typical UG duration","value":"\\u2248 5.5 Years (incl. internship) \\u2022 varies"},{"key":"Where you work","value":"AYUSH hospitals \\u2022 Clinics \\u2022 Wellness centres"},{"key":"Reality check","value":"Clinical maturity + patient trust decide success"}]	[]	\N	\N	[]	[]	[]	26	t	2026-07-23 17:52:25	2026-07-25 04:30:50	30	52	63	64	courses/medical/ayush	[]	[]	{}	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[{"title": "AYUSH Hospitals & Dispensaries", "description": "Clinical roles in government/private AYUSH setups."}, {"title": "Clinics & Private Practice", "description": "Independent practice (as per registration rules and experience)."}, {"title": "Wellness & Lifestyle Centres", "description": "Holistic health, preventive care, therapy/wellness programs."}, {"title": "Teaching & Research (with PG)", "description": "Academic track in recognised colleges and research institutions."}]	["Choose a recognised college with strong clinical exposure and hospital tie-up.", "Understand the system's philosophy and treatment approach before committing.", "Long-term success depends on clinical maturity, ethics and patient trust building."]	["Class 10 & 12 marksheets", "ID proof (Aadhaar etc.)", "Photo + signature", "Category/EWS/Income certificate (if applicable)", "Domicile (if required)", "Medical fitness certificate (if asked by institute/counselling)"]	["Strong basics in biology and patient communication", "Ethics + discipline + long-term learning mindset", "Case history-taking and follow-up discipline (very important in AYUSH practice)", "Practical exposure during internship (seriously, not just attendance)", "If you want teaching/research, plan PG (MD) early"]	[]	["Usually after Class 12 with Science (commonly PCB); exact criteria varies by system and regulations.", "Admissions may be via NEET (UG) or other criteria depending on current rules and notifications.", "Medical fitness and document verification apply as per counselling rules.", "Always confirm recognition of the college and the course before admission."]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[{"focus": "Foundation in the chosen AYUSH system + clinical training as per syllabus.", "title": "UG AYUSH Degree (BAMS / BHMS / BUMS / BSMS)", "duration": "Typically 5.5 Years (including internship) • varies by system"}, {"focus": "Work in clinics/hospitals/wellness setups; build practical patient-handling experience.", "title": "Clinical Practice / Service", "duration": "Continuous"}, {"focus": "Advanced learning for teaching, research, and specialised practice tracks.", "title": "PG Specialisation (MD in AYUSH system)", "duration": "Typically 3 Years (varies)"}, {"focus": "Senior clinician, teaching roles, research, administration, wellness entrepreneurship (as per experience).", "title": "Long-term growth", "duration": "Continuous"}]	[{"key": "ayurveda", "badge": "Traditional Indian Medicine", "title": "Ayurveda (BAMS → MD Ayurveda)", "bestFor": "Students interested in traditional Indian medicine, holistic lifestyle approach and long-term clinical practice building.", "commonRoute": ["BAMS (UG)", "Internship (as per norms)", "MD Ayurveda (PG)"], "whatYouStudy": "Ayurvedic principles, diagnosis methods, herbal formulations, Panchakarma basics (where applicable) and clinical practice as per syllabus.", "whereYouWork": ["AYUSH hospitals", "Clinics", "Wellness centres", "Panchakarma centres", "Research/teaching (with PG)"]}, {"key": "homeopathy", "badge": "Alternative Medicine System", "title": "Homoeopathy (BHMS → MD Homoeopathy)", "bestFor": "Students who like detailed patient history-taking and long-term case management style practice.", "commonRoute": ["BHMS (UG)", "Internship (as per norms)", "MD Homoeopathy (PG)"], "whatYouStudy": "Homeopathic philosophy, materia medica, repertory, case-taking, clinical training and practice systems as per syllabus.", "whereYouWork": ["Homeopathy hospitals", "Clinics", "Dispensaries", "Private practice", "Teaching/research (with PG)"]}, {"key": "unani", "badge": "Greco-Arab Medicine System", "title": "Unani (BUMS → MD Unani)", "bestFor": "Students interested in Unani philosophy, regimen-based care and clinical practice in AYUSH setups.", "commonRoute": ["BUMS (UG)", "Internship (as per norms)", "MD Unani (PG)"], "whatYouStudy": "Unani principles, diagnosis, regimens, pharmacology (as per Unani), and clinical training as per syllabus.", "whereYouWork": ["AYUSH hospitals", "Unani clinics", "Dispensaries", "Community health programs", "Teaching (with PG)"]}, {"key": "siddha", "badge": "Traditional South Indian System", "title": "Siddha (BSMS → MD Siddha)", "bestFor": "Students interested in Siddha system and long-term clinical practice building in recognised setups.", "commonRoute": ["BSMS (UG)", "Internship (as per norms)", "MD Siddha (PG)"], "whatYouStudy": "Siddha principles, medicines, diagnosis methods, and clinical training as per syllabus.", "whereYouWork": ["Siddha hospitals/clinics", "AYUSH wellness centres", "Community health (where applicable)", "Teaching (with PG)"]}]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]
29	About B.Arch	B.Arch (Bachelor of Architecture) is a professional degree focused on building design, spatial planning, construction techniques and architectural creativity. The course is studio-intensive and requires a balance of creativity, technical knowledge and practical site understanding.	The course is studio-intensive and requires a balance of creativity, technical knowledge and practical site understanding.	[\n        {"key":"Degree type","value":"Professional Architecture Degree"},\n        {"key":"Duration","value":"5 Years"},\n        {"key":"Eligibility","value":"Class 12 with Mathematics"},\n        {"key":"Entry exams","value":"NATA / JEE-based (as applicable)"},\n        {"key":"Career scope","value":"Design • Construction • Planning • Practice"}\n    ]	[]	\N	\N	[]	[]	[]	29	t	2026-07-23 18:53:09	2026-07-23 18:54:28	30	66	67	69	courses/barch	[]	[]	{}	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[{"icon": "Landmark", "title": "Architectural Firms", "description": "Design studios, drafting, project coordination and client-facing roles."}, {"icon": "Ruler", "title": "Construction & Infrastructure", "description": "Site supervision, execution coordination, quality and planning."}, {"icon": "Building2", "title": "Urban Planning / Govt Projects", "description": "Town planning bodies, development authorities, public projects."}, {"icon": "Briefcase", "title": "Independent Practice / Consultancy", "description": "Private practice after registration and experience."}]	[]	["Class 10 & 12 marksheets", "Mathematics proof in Class 12", "Entrance exam scorecard (NATA/JEE-based as applicable)", "ID proof (Aadhaar etc.)", "Photo + signature", "Category/Domicile certificate (if applicable)"]	["Strong drawing, sketching and visualisation skills", "Design thinking and creativity", "Software skills (AutoCAD, SketchUp, BIM tools over time)", "Site exposure and material understanding", "Communication skills for client and team interaction"]	[]	["Class 12 passed with Mathematics as