31	About BCA	BCA (Bachelor of Computer Applications) is an undergraduate programme focused on computer applications, programming and software fundamentals. It is a popular route for students who want to enter IT without pursuing B.Tech. Your career outcome depends heavily on skills: projects, internships, coding practice and real software exposure matter more than marks alone.	Your career outcome depends heavily on skills: projects, internships, coding practice and real software exposure matter more than marks alone.	[\n        {"key":"Degree type","value":"UG Computer Applications Degree"},\n        {"key":"Duration","value":"3 Years"},\n        {"key":"Eligibility","value":"Class 12 (criteria varies)"},\n        {"key":"Best for","value":"Software careers without Engineering"},\n        {"key":"Strong ladder","value":"BCA → MCA → specialisation"}\n    ]	[]	\N	\N	[]	[]	[]	31	t	2026-07-23 18:56:07	2026-07-23 18:57:27	30	66	71	72	courses/bca	[]	[]	{}	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[{"icon": "Cpu", "title": "Software / IT Services", "description": "Web/app development, support, testing and tech services roles."}, {"icon": "Briefcase", "title": "Product Companies / Startups", "description": "Developer roles if you have strong projects and interview readiness."}, {"icon": "Database", "title": "Data & Database Teams", "description": "DB support, data operations, analytics support roles (with skills)."}, {"icon": "Network", "title": "Networking / IT Operations", "description": "IT support, systems and basic networking operations roles."}]	["Choose a college with good computer labs, faculty and internship support.", "Check if they include modern development skills or only theory.", "Ask about placement support, alumni outcomes and practical project work."]	["Class 10 & 12 marksheets", "ID proof (Aadhaar etc.)", "Photo + signature", "Category/EWS/Income certificate (if applicable)", "Domicile (if required)"]	["Learn one programming language well (Java/Python/JS)", "Bui