34	About M.Sc Computer Science / IT	M.Sc Computer Science / IT is a postgraduate science degree that deepens your understanding of computer science fundamentals and advanced topics. It often has stronger theory + research orientation compared to many UG routes. Your project/dissertation is a key output in M.Sc — it can support both industry roles and research/PhD readiness depending on how you plan it.	Your project/dissertation is a key output in M.Sc — it can support both industry roles and research/PhD readiness depending on how you plan it.	[\n        {"key":"Degree type","value":"PG Science Degree (CS/IT)"},\n        {"key":"Duration","value":"2 Years (varies)"},\n        {"key":"Eligibility","value":"Relevant UG degree (criteria varies)"},\n        {"key":"Best for","value":"Deeper CS • research • stronger specialization"},\n        {"key":"Reality check","value":"Project + skills decide outcomes"}\n    ]	[]	\N	\N	[]	[]	[]	34	t	2026-07-23 19:01:43	2026-07-23 19:02:37	30	66	71	75	courses/msc	[]	[]	{}	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[]	[{"icon": "Cpu", "title": "IT Services & Software", "description": "Development, testing, support, implementation roles (with skills)."}, {"icon": "Database", "title": "Data / Database Teams", "description": "Analytics support, data ops, SQL/reporting roles (with skills)."}, {"icon": "Network", "title": "Systems / Networking", "description": "Network/system support, infrastructure roles (with skills)."}, {"icon": "FlaskConical", "title": "Research / Academia (as per norms)", "description": "RA roles, labs, teaching track, PhD pathway (depends on eligibility)."}]	["Check electives and lab facilities—those decide your specialisation options.", "Choose a dissertation/project topic aligned with your target career.", "If your goal is industry, build projects and internship exposure alongside academics."]	["UG marksheets + degree/provisional certificate", "Entrance scorecard (if applicable)", "ID proof (Aadhaar etc.)", "Photo + signatur